# Aokigahara free-roam — binary handling.
#
# The intended Git LFS ruleset is preserved verbatim in .gitattributes.lfs.
# It is NOT active here: the environment in which this repository was first
# published cannot reach lfs.github.com (blocked at the egress gateway), so the
# binary assets are stored as ordinary Git objects to guarantee they are not
# lost. Every file is well under GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit; the largest is
# 29.8 MB and the whole tree is about 240 MB.
#
# To switch to LFS from a machine that can reach lfs.github.com:
#     bash tools/enable_lfs.sh
#
# Until then, mark binaries so Git never attempts text diffing or EOL rewriting.
*.glb   binary
*.gltf  binary
*.fbx   binary
*.blend binary
*.obj   binary
*.exr   binary
*.hdr   binary
*.tif   binary
*.tiff  binary
*.f32   binary
*.u8    binary
*.npz   binary
*.bin   binary
*.zip   binary
*.7z    binary
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.webp  binary
# Keep every text asset diffable, but never rewrite line endings: the recovered
# research data and the SHA-256-verified manifests must stay byte-exact.
*.json    -text
*.csv     -text
*.geojson -text
*.html    -text
*.md      -text
*.js      -text
*.mjs     -text
*.py      -text
